domain ADR0033Review:
  description "Formal review of ADR0033 revision one and implementation-design revision six."

problem P1:
  |
    Determine whether removing provider transport and worker execution Config revision
    identities or snapshots from durable run identity breaks accepted retry,
    accounting, fencing, late-result, technical-outcome, or time-boundary contracts.

evidence E1:
  |
    The reviewed authoritative ADR0033 SHA256 is
    ae8b736857b59188880acbf397e2da941caf5c102539b2410ddd7011fd1f529a.

evidence E2:
  |
    The reviewed implementation-design revision-six SHA256 is
    a0f2ba909d3c71fb7de2235bd84125b420663f6f8b5400c4236eaf92e832ebff.

evidence E3:
  |
    Accepted foundation requirements permit a failed attempt to end and an explicit
    retry to create a new attempt reconstructed from retained source and applicable
    authorized input. They do not require intermediate candidate, context, or checkpoint
    persistence.

evidence E4:
  |
    Accepted ADR0032 requires separate provider transport and worker execution time
    controls, monotonic accounting, fenced rejection of late results, and typed technical
    outcomes. It leaves exact values and exact runtime policy acceptance pending.

evidence E5:
  |
    Design revision six removes both Config identities from SemanticAuthoringRunV1 but
    retains source identity, semantic policy, pricing and token-estimator identities,
    provider request identity and state, reservations, receipts, monotonic accounting,
    execution fencing, technical outcomes, predecessor linkage, and source-based new-run
    reconstruction.

evidence E6:
  |
    One independent reviewer and the primary review found no P0 through P3 defect. Both
    verified that the supplied candidate digests remained unchanged after review.

premise C1:
  |
    A new retry run need not reproduce an old execution Config unless an accepted exact
    replay, compliance, billing, or service-level requirement says otherwise. No such
    accepted requirement was identified in the reviewed scope.

pending U1:
  |
    The implementation must retain a durable claim or expiry fact sufficient to decide
    worker-lease expiry after restart without consulting a changed runtime Config. Exact
    DDL belongs to the implementation slice, so this does not require a Config identity
    or snapshot and is not a current design blocker.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, E5, E6, C1, U1:
  |
    Complete REVIEW with PASS and no P0, P1, P2, or P3 findings. Carry U1 as an
    implementation-stage verification obligation. This review is not owner acceptance
    and does not authorize implementation, commit, push, provider calls, deployment,
    migration, activation, or release.
